74}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3506a439-f9a0-5eea-8755-aa700aeade50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246274} :answer-field/id #uuid "62622aa7-e1cf-55da-b818-fd1f375b01ac" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246273} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a021f82-10e6-5f67-a6ab-3e3700462e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a021f82-10e6-5f67-a6ab-3e3700462e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246276} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b35370-e488-5af6-84c7-3888fd94c5a4" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246275}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cbcf0be-5a30-5a56-a240-3ef74e9e741b" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167631" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nCurrent part:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-5}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/96bd60d23237f836b77a26c5c0461a5c2a474554f0a14266b53fc5e7d999f1b7.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $sin⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f050d6ac-c929-5c48-80a3-5946d7e5cf0c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum and Minimum Values of a Vertically Translated Sine or Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5feb501-f60a-5019-9e82-340fe0d6a961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5feb501-f60a-5019-9e82-340fe0d6a961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246279} :answer-field/id #uuid "02f6e93b-5a17-558b-a6b5-7460fd4eb482" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246278}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a9e807d-bfca-58e5-8c84-64c886bddc34" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167632" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n* Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n* Then, shift it by $1$ units **up**.\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/dbe1701a42a160e982bff96b1085727080c39b87ca2c99886e3e153e2f5964cc.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is $y=2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe know that $y=sin⁡x$ has a maximum value of $1.$ \n\n$$\nsin⁡x\\le 1\n$$\n\nAdding $1$ to both sides of the above inequality gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡x+1\\le 1+1 \\\\ sin⁡x+1\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $sin⁡x+1$ is $A=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3e26d07-1a98-5c57-8891-03c2ab7d33b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Parameter Given the Graph of a Stretched Sine or Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79b5e06e-4a3c-55c9-95fa-e436144f813f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79b5e06e-4a3c-55c9-95fa-e436144f813f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246282} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2192b5-5f17-53c9-9fe3-db2b99eca7e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246281}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23875acc-b2db-580b-a704-1ad7917050ac" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167633" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $B,$ we first need to find the period of the function.\n\nThe graph shows that the function makes $3$ complete cycles on the interval $[0,2\\pi ].$ So, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/544997dc11f7c88d5aa7b3f78d8dd1059a0ac08092726983897c5992d03acf8b.png)\n\n \n\nWe know that for the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ the horizontal scaling factor is $\\frac{1}{B},$ and the period is multiplied by the scaling factor:\n\n$$\n\\text{period}=2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{B}\n$$\n\nFor our function, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\pi }{3} & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{B} \\\\ \\frac{2\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{B} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{1}{B} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "add45606-39f6-5a61-9535-867d2950d183" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Constant Factor Rule to Integrate a Power Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "760f980d-7bdf-5fd4-b47b-850ef11f594f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "760f980d-7bdf-5fd4-b47b-850ef11f594f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246285} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4a501a-4a94-552f-bc25-6a36422dbbb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246284}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4202f39e-d752-5bc7-9691-e451845d6a3e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167634" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$" :question/worked-solution "We take the constant factor out of the integral and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{(-2+1)}}{-2+1})+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{-1})+C \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {x}^{-1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5caf8f3d-8197-500a-91a3-e161d87f58ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5caf8f3d-8197-500a-91a3-e161d87f58ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246288} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bef787b-2bf0-5acc-b0d3-ae5427b61e92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246287}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4076a52-a47a-59ca-ae7e-394d426e5542" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167635" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nGiven that $A=2$ and $B=3,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C.$" :question/worked-solution "We found that $A=2$ and $B=3$ in steps 2 and 3, respectively. Hence, $f(x)={x}^{3}+2x.$ \n\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules and our result from step 4, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-\\frac{2}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b7d0153-6e0a-5e19-83f1-960811dc5205" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23a552bf-4600-5789-8d0d-864502a7a65b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^x-3x^2-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23a552bf-4600-5789-8d0d-864502a7a65b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^x-3x^2-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246291} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb103371-9571-590d-9fc5-4a5943c0f3c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39f12ac5-2c04-5851-ba29-604a494f45a9" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167636" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nGiven that $A=2$ and $B=3,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nIf $k(x)=g(x)-f(x),$ where $A=2$ and $B=3,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "We found that $A=2$ and $B=3$ in steps 3 and 4, respectively. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =g(x)-f(x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{x}-({x}^{3}+2x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the addition and power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf184429-45f7-56f5-847d-b30740acca76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf184429-45f7-56f5-847d-b30740acca76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246294} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8856d5a-a811-5a92-b698-cb77c5846fed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246293}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3216cd3-d584-5683-925d-487020d5efaf" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167637" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nGiven that $A=2$ and $B=3,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C.$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nIf $k(x)=g(x)-f(x),$ where $A=2$ and $B=3,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3e^x-3x^2-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind $m,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have $k(x)=3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x.$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to ${k}^{′}(0).$ From step 6, the derivative is\n\n$$\n{k}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{′}(0) & =3{e}^{0}-3(0)^{2}-2 \\\\  & =3-0-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef24524d-3d5c-5da1-a8f6-66387279901d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef24524d-3d5c-5da1-a8f6-66387279901d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246297} :answer-field/id #uuid "9759300c-3800-5d8e-9efb-680474198464" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246296}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6b7b08f-24b1-5b68-a5ec-d550db474ce4" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-167638" :question/problem "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nGiven that $A=2$ and $B=3,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x-\\frac{2}{x}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C.$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nIf $k(x)=g(x)-f(x),$ where $A=2$ and $B=3,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3e^x-3x^2-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\nFind $m,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0$ intersects the $x$-axis at $(c,0).$ Find the value of $c.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $c=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have $k(x)=3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x.$ In step 7, we found that the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is $m=1.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate of the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=k(0)=3{e}^{(0)}-(0)^{3}-2(0)=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =(1)(x-0) \\\\ y-3 & =x \\\\ y & =x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $x$-intercept of this tangent line, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ 0 & =x+3 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(-3,0),$ and we have $c=-3.$"}]}
